window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>FREE THE CROWS, FALLON, AND THEY WILL MAKE YOU QUEEN.</b></p> <p>Until an oracle predicted my regal future, I'd never imagined myself rising above the curve of my round ears. After all, I was the magicless halfling loved by beasts but loathed by every pure-blooded faerie at court. Well . . . by all but one.</p> <p>Dante Regio, prince of Luce, had owned my heart since he gave me my first kiss. If gathering a slew of iron relics could help me overthrow the current monarch and crown his brother to rule at my side, then treasure hunting I'd go.</p> <p>If only the oracle had warned me what winged demon I was releasing into the world.</p> <p>And that I'd become this demon's obsession.</p> <p><i>Fans of Sarah J. Maas and Mary E. Pearson will devour this epic fantasy romance full of deceit, betrayal, and false loves that could swallow a person whole.</i></p> <p>Adapted from the novel and produced with a full cast of actors, immersive sound effects and cinematic music!</p> <p>Narrated by Thea Wolfe, with performances by Henry Kramer as Dante, Danny Gavigan as Antoni, Matt Bassett as Morrgot, Rayner Gabriel as Marco, Anthony Palmini as Phoebus, Sandi Stock as Nonna, Stephanie Németh-Parker as Giana, Jonathan Lee Taylor as Ptolemy Timeus, and Kimberly Gilbert as Mamma. Also with Andrew James Spooner, Nora Achrati, Elena Anderson, Kelly Baskin, Mike Carnes, Danielle Cohen, David Cui Cui, Colleen Delany, Wyn Delano, Ian DePriest, Drew Kopas, Donald Guzzi, Laura C. Harris, Ryan Huagen, James Konicheck, Erin Lin, Daniel Llaca, Joe Mallon, Rob McFadyen, Emlyn McFarland, Christopher McLinden, Brad Smith, Joey Sourlis, Christopher Tester, Yasmin Tuazon, Christopher Walker, and others.</p>"; 
